Description: Keep the focus on a sticky window when switching workspaces
 A focused sticky floating window lost the focus when another workspace
 was focused on the same output, even an empty one, although it stays
 visible there; i3 keeps it focused. Sway also drew every sticky
 floating window with focused decorations after the switch. The sticky
 window now keeps the focus and the focus stack, and floating windows no
 longer inherit the workspace's focused state for their decorations.
 .
 Taken from the open upstream pull request (both commits squashed),
 carried until it is merged. Adapted to 1.11: upstream master's
 last_workspace is the new output's previously active workspace
 (upstream commit 3cb86e4a, not in 1.11 or 1.12), which 1.11 calls
 new_output_last_ws, so the check uses that. Focusing a workspace on
 another output still moves the focus there.
